---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  navKey="support"
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with Deptheos: documentation, GitHub Discussions, public bug reports, and email support for diagnostics and private files."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Deptheos is free and open source. Help comes through GitHub for anything that can be
      public, and by email for anything that can't.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section id="where">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where to ask</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>How do I…?</strong> The <a href="/docs/">docs</a> cover every part of the app, and
          <a href="/docs/faq/">Questions and answers</a> and <a href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Troubleshooting</a>
          handle the most common issues. Questions the docs don't answer go to
          <a href="https://github.com/ryanmitts/deptheos/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Something doesn't work, or it crashed.</strong> Open a
          <a href="https://github.com/ryanmitts/deptheos/issues/new?template=bug.yml">bug report</a> on GitHub
          (Help ▸ <em>Report a Problem…</em> in the desktop app opens it). Say what you did, what you expected, and
          what happened. Issues are public—don't attach diagnostics, crash reports, or private photos there. Email
          them instead (see below).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An idea for the app.</strong> A
          <a href="https://github.com/ryanmitts/deptheos/issues/new?template=feature.yml">feature request</a>
          on GitHub.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Diagnostics, and anything private.</strong> Email
          <a href="mailto:support@deptheos.com">support@deptheos.com</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A security problem.</strong> Report it privately, as the
          <a href="https://github.com/ryanmitts/deptheos/security/policy">security policy</a> says, not in a
          public issue.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="diagnostics">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Sending diagnostics</h2>
      <p>
        The diagnostics are one zip file of the app's recent logs and, on the desktop, its crash reports. They
        say what the app was doing when something went wrong, which is usually what it takes to fix it. Your home
        folder is written as <code>~</code> in the logs, but they name the files and folders the app read, so the
        file goes by email, never on a public issue. <a href="/privacy/#diagnostics">Privacy</a> says what it
        holds and what is done with it.
      </p>
      <h3 id="desktop">On a Mac, Windows or Linux</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          To capture more detail, turn on Settings ▸ Advanced ▸ <em>Verbose logging</em> (it lasts until Deptheos
          quits), and do what went wrong again.
        </li>
        <li>
          Choose Help ▸ <em>Save Diagnostics…</em> and pick where to save the zip. On Windows and Linux the Help
          menu is under the menu (≡) button.
        </li>
        <li>
          Email the zip to <a href="mailto:support@deptheos.com">support@deptheos.com</a>, with what you did and
          what happened, or a link to the bug report you opened.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h3 id="ios">On iPhone and iPad</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>In the Library, tap Settings, then Diagnostics.</li>
        <li>To capture more detail, turn on <em>Verbose logging</em> and do what went wrong again.</li>
        <li>
          Tap <em>Send Diagnostics…</em>. The share sheet opens with the zip: choose Mail and send it to
          <a href="mailto:support@deptheos.com">support@deptheos.com</a>, with what you did and what happened.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h3 id="cli">The command line tool</h3>
      <p>
        <code>deptheos</code> logs to the terminal only. Copy what it printed into the bug report, or set
        <code>RUST_LOG=debug</code> for more detail.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
